{
  "id": "v3.initial_preplan_recovery",
  "version": "1",
  "description": "Existing Runtime lifecycle design for an accepted request that must bind its original control, reach a ready plan or a typed terminal disposition while existing health probes recover, dispatch only a ready plan, and close out with one internal request disposition receipt. Probe start or completion is not health success and cannot substitute for normal candidate eligibility; this graph requires no probe handoff or immediate first-poll recheck. Request-local recovery waits do not acquire business capacity or renew the original residence deadline; attempt exhaustion must not block a normal, legal untried tier/default identity.",
